# AutoDub repo rules

## Public vs local

This repo is intended to be **public**. Never commit:

| Path / pattern | Why |
| --- | --- |
| `.env` | API keys |
| `operator/` | COST, DECISIONS, real cast/voice IDs, live HANDOFFs, media paths |
| `holdout/` | Blind acceptance — verifier-only; implementer must not read or edit |
| Episode media / stems / renders | `*.mkv`, `*.mp4`, `*.wav`, `*.mka`, cache dirs (see `.gitignore`) |

`.env.example` stays empty of secrets (key names only). If a key was pasted into `.env.example`, move it to `.env` and clear the example before any commit.

`cast/examples/` may ship **schema + fake IDs only**. Real One Piece (etc.) bindings live under `operator/cast/`.

## Blind verification

- Behaviour contract: `docs/CONTRACT.md` (public).
- Implementer writes code + `tests/` only.
- Verifier owns `holdout/` (local/gitignored). Do not show holdout source to the implementer.
- Failures reported as **behaviour**, not test source.
- Greens may be promoted into `tests/audit/` (public regression).

## Cross-agent continuity

- Before fanning or pausing a worker, write/update `operator/handoffs/<stream>-HANDOFF.md` from `docs/HANDOFF.template.md`.
- Workers update the same HANDOFF before exit.
- Chat reads HANDOFFs on resume — do not rely on chat scroll alone.
- Never put API keys or real voice IDs in public docs or commit messages.

## Product invariants (while building)

- When EN captions exist: spoken text = caption text (no invented lines).
- Do not redistribute episode files or AutoDub masters from this project.
- Do not add DRM decryption / stream-ripping helpers.
- Prefer prior-art glue over rewriting dub pipelines from scratch.

## Commits

- Commit public engine/docs/rules freely.
- Never `git add -f` on `.env`, `operator/`, or `holdout/`.
- Before push: `git status` and confirm those paths are absent.
